      "role": "user",
      "content": "i get that it's complex, but isn't it a bit of a stretch to say \"bodily autonomy\" is a valid argument when the science is so clear? i mean, if someone's choice puts everyone else at risk, doesn't the \"legitimate concern\" part kind of disappear? feels like saying it was a \"debate\" treats actual science like it was just another opinion.",
